Spec: Formal Android connection execution

Purpose:
  Execute retained caller-bound public connection operations through authenticated direct-first transports and one-use descriptors.

Owns:
  ./FormalConnections.java

References:
  /agent-core/src/main/java/dev/linkgate/agent/ConnectionJournal.sdd
  /transport-core/src/main/java/dev/linkgate/transport/ConnectionPlanner.sdd

Must:
  Require configured server authority and an owner-started host before opening; preserve original admission through journal, authorization, candidates and peer handshakes.
  Use only reviewed endpoints and current exact local/server grants; candidate selection cannot widen the request or replay payload.
  Share bounded host executors and private runtime leases with experimental streams, keep at most `32` retained runtime entries and `16` per caller, and retain failed persistence entries rather than growing unbounded.
  Attach only an atomically consumed caller/boot-bound claim, require descriptor acknowledgement within ten seconds and close on caller death or authority loss.
  Count payload only after successful directional writes, observe real FIN/drain and persist cumulative terminal state after aborting IO.
  Reject stale generation completions, close affected streams on network change and report the original selected path and incomplete counters after failures.
